<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/inventions?focus=hovercraft">Inventions &amp; Discoveries</a> · Transport and navigation</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hovercraft</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1937">1937</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Air-cushion vehicle, ACV</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">A hovercraft is an amphibious craft that rides on a cushion of air blown under its hull, so that it can travel over land, water, mud and ice. The Swedish scientist <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emanuel-swedenborg">Emanuel Swedenborg</a> mentioned hovering in 1716, and John Isaac Thornycroft patented an early air-cushion ship design in the 1870s. The Finnish engineer Toivo J. Kaario built the prototype Pintaliitäjä in 1937, with a lift engine blowing air into a flexible envelope. Christopher Cockerell developed the ring of air and a successful skirt, and the SR.N1 first hovered on 11 June 1959 and crossed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/english-channel">English Channel</a> on 25 July 1959.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hovercraft.jpg" alt="Hovercraft" width="330" height="264" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Petty Officer 2nd Class Michael D. Degner, U.S. Navy · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:LCAC_19970620.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="inv-entry"><h2 class="enc-section-title">On the inventions tree</h2><dl class="inv-entry-facts"><div><dt>First known</dt><dd>1937</dd></div><div><dt>Where</dt><dd>Finland</dd></div><div><dt>Credited to</dt><dd>Toivo J. Kaario · Christopher Cockerell</dd></div></dl><p class="inv-entry-note"><span class="inv-k">Note</span>Christopher Cockerell's group is credited with the first successful skirt and the first practical vehicle, the SR.N1 of 1959. Thornycroft patented an early design in the 1870s, but suitable engines did not yet exist.</p><div class="inv-entry-rel"><span class="inv-k">Built on</span><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/internal-combustion-engine">Internal combustion engine<span>1794</span></a></div><p class="enc-article-foot"><a class="enc-random-link" href="/inventions?focus=hovercraft">See it on the inventions tree &rarr;</a></p></section>
